Z||000000||Wolfhound||03-29-2001||10:53 AM||||Well I,ve come pretty close to being finished with the 84. cleaned power window and mirror switches with WD40 and compressed air, added radio, rebuilt console, and cleaned. Take a look!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/atrf.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/atlr.JPG">  <BR>I was asked if the wheels were hub caps or aluminum, on closer inspection they are nether, They are steel with an aluminum insert.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/atw.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/atd.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ati.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alri.JPG">  <BR>Used the simulated leather wheel from a 85 SE the leather GT wheel will live elsewhere.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/atsw.JPG"> <BR>Not bad for a hundred bucks! As We say down South "Even a blind pig can find an acorn every once in a while." <p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||6
